      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent sublimation can often stem from underlying thermal instability or improper material preparation rather than just the set temperature. Since your pressure is steady, the issue might be fluctuating ambient temperatures in the Vietnam factory or variability in the substrate thickness affecting heat transfer. It is also possible that the film powder isn't fully fused due to uneven heating, which requires calibrating your Kilopack or checking if the substrate has proper张口 to absorb the ink. I recommend double-checking the porosity of your materials and ensuring no moisture contamination is interfering with the heat cycle.",
