    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We checked the moisture and the substrate seems fine. The weird thing is, it's not a consistent fade across the whole sheet. It's like... random patches of color just vanish. One minute a logo is solid, the next minute there's a patch where the ink just seems to have disappeared into thin air during the press. It's almost like something is actively pulling the pigment away from the fabric. Is there any chemical reason why the ink would move or vanish like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
