    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, so maybe it's a hot spot issue, but the patterns are so irregular it doesn't feel like a mechanical failure in the heater. It’s like the ink is being snatched away at specific, unpredictable moments. It feels much more intentional than just a temperature fluctuation. Is there any scenario in sublimation where the pigment just... disappears, like it's been interfered with by something outside of the normal chemical process?",
